==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{l|ru|су-}} + *тъка (related to  {{l|ru|ты́кать}}), resulting in {{m|ru|[[стык]] [[день|дня]] [[и]] [[ночь|но́чи]]||union of day and night}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|су́тки}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-сутки.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|су́тки|f*|or|су́тки|m*|sgtail=*|pltail=*|notes=* Proscribed.|adj=су́точный}}

# [[24]] [[hours]] (of the clock), [[day]], day and night, [[nychthemeron]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[круглый|кру́глые]] '''су́тки'''|round '''the clock'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[за]] '''су́тки'''|during the day/ for the day, during 24 hours / for 24 hours}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[ме́нее]], [[чем]] [[за]] '''су́тки'''|less than 24 hours}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1935|author=w:ru:Андрей Платонов<t:{{w|Andrei Platonov}}>|title=w:ru:[[Джан (повесть)|Джан]]|chapter=3|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=Robert and Elizabeth Chandler|title2=w:[[Soul (novel)|Soul]]|location2=London|publisher2=w:en:[[Harvill Secker|Harvill Press]]|year2=2003|page2=|pageurl2=|text=По́езд давно́ поки́нул Москву́; прошло́ уже́ не́сколько '''су́ток''' езды́.|t=The train had long ago left Moscow behind; several '''days and nights''' of travel had already passed by.}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|су́тки|f*|or|су́тки|m*|sgtail=*|pltail=*|notes=* Proscribed.}}

